  "body": "Shares the project's Claude Code agents and skills through the repo, so every checkout (and every contributor using Claude Code) gets the same ones.\n\n**Tracked now**\n- `.claude/agents/gate-runner.md` - runs a verification gate and reports pass/fail per binary.\n- `.claude/agents/graph-updater.md` - refreshes the graphify knowledge graph.\n- `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md` - reviews one PR, comment only, in its own worktree.\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md` - finds fork PRs with an unreviewed head and dispatches PR-reviewer, one at a time.\n\n**Still ignored** (`.gitignore`): `/.claude/*` except `agents/` and `skills/`, so `settings.json`, `settings.local.json`, `worktrees/`, `scheduled_tasks.lock`, `pr-review.lock` and anything else Claude Code writes stay local; `*.lock` under `.claude` is ignored everywhere.\n\n**Edited for sharing**: the files hard-coded `C:\\Users\\...\\Claude-001`; they now use the repo root (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`) and \"the main checkout\". No secrets in any file (read before publishing).\n\nNot included: the user-level `gh-issues` skill (lives in `~/.claude/skills`, not in this repo), which AGENTS.md tells agents to load.\n\nChangelog: none (tooling/docs only)\n",
